But since you're starting with a big two-handed weapon, getting
Cleaver in Minetown certainly isn't a bad turn. I find it totally
worth using to the end of the quest (including spending a scroll of
enchant weapon or two on it). 
It's a relatively weak end-game weapon, but i prefer not to spend all
my early game streamlining everything for the ultimate ascension kit.
If i wanted to indulge in sick ultra-sacrifice fests until i got the
Ultimate Divine Gift, i could play ADOM.

> I know that ultimately, you want to be wielding two weapons, or one
> weapon and a shield, instead of a two handed weapon, but isn't the
> Cleaver very useful since barbarians are guaranteed it as a first gift?

I find it very useful for the time you're likely to get your hands on
it. The earlier, the better, of course.

